<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $55.6 mln Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $55.6 mln Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $55.6 million surplus on Jan 10 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JANUARY 10</p>
<p>Exports: $226 million</p>
<p>Imports: $190.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $199.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $179.9 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $55.6 million</p>
<p>JANUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.419 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.528 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.766 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.406 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $251 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
